artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider a cross-silo federated learning setting in which a finite collection of organizations (silos) S_1, ..., S_N jointly train a shared model without centralizing their data. Each silo S_i holds a local dataset D_i and operates under its own constraints. Formally, model the system as a tuple (S, D, A, P, V) where:

- S = {S_1, ..., S_N} is the set of participating silos.
- D = {D_1, ..., D_N}: each D_i is generated and labeled using a silo-specific (heterogeneous) data pipeline; the marginal feature distributions and label schemas may differ across silos.
- A = {A_1, ..., A_N}: each A_i is the software/runtime stack of silo S_i; the A_i may be mutually incompatible (different ML frameworks, hardware accelerators, versions, OS environments).
- P = {P_1, ..., P_N}: each P_i encodes jurisdiction-dependent data-use approvals and policy constraints (e.g., legal restrictions on which fields of D_i may be used, exported, encrypted, logged, or combined with data from other silos), and the global system must run a policy-enforcing infrastructure that provably respects P_i for every silo at every step of training and inference.
- V is a vertical-partitioning structure: the global feature space F = F_1 ∪ ... ∪ F_N is partitioned (possibly with overlap) so that silo S_i observes only features F_i over its records; some entities are shared across silos but identified by different keys, and some features required for a record may be missing.

Design a coordination protocol and accompanying system architecture that jointly accomplishes all of the following:
(a) trains a global predictive model f_θ on the union of silo data while honoring every policy P_i;
(b) reconciles heterogeneous data generation and labeling pipelines so that local datasets D_i contribute consistently to f_θ;
(c) interoperates across the incompatible software stacks A_i without requiring uniform infrastructure;
(d) performs private entity alignment across silos so that records corresponding to the same underlying entity can be linked under vertical partitioning without revealing non-matching identifiers;
(e) handles missing features (records present in some F_i but absent in others) in a principled statistical manner;
(f) provides verifiable enforcement of the per-silo policies P_i throughout the protocol.

Give such a protocol together with formal guarantees of correctness, privacy/policy compliance, communication and computation efficiency, and statistical utility of the resulting model f_θ, or prove impossibility results delimiting which combinations of (a)–(f) can be simultaneously achieved.
